    "objective": "Resolves VAL-07 and VAL-12 \u2014 the same attribution defect from both directions, hit independently in three validation runs. The R/W matrix attributes primed variables to the syntactic primer, so (a) wrapper actions that prime a variable only through a helper operator vanish from the matrix (9 CLI actions collapsed to 4 on taskq), and (b) helper operators are listed AS actions while composed actions whose writes happen entirely through called operators or UNCHANGED get no column (MarkExternal listed, RunFulfillmentWorker absent, on distributed_history). Dense-row fractions, dense columns, action_count, component action counts \u2014 and the fitness facts derived from them \u2014 are computed over a partially wrong action set. Fix: attribute primes to the top-level action disjuncts (Next/ExternalNext members), expanding called-operator bodies transitively (the CD-01/F1 resolution machinery, extended by CD-05); helpers are not actions. Regression tests covering both shapes, failing pre-fix; verify against the real distributed_history External view and record the corrected matrix as evidence.\n",
